sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: stage 5 of the command development pipeline (feature-flow section 6, gateway-recovery "Automatic releases"). A merged green commit gets an automatic Swamp release run when automatic releases are enabled and unpaused; a failed check switches back. The steps of the run itself are in the chart gateway:release:deploy. No fleet test follows a release.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 5 · automatic Swamp release
  %% kind: pipeline.5-automatic-release
  autonumber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=CI tone=blue
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane GN icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>main · CI
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>release run
  participant GN as Gateway Node<br/>code · services
  Note over GW,GH: Find newest green commit<br/>on main · CI
  %%> Built:
  %%> - the Gateway looks every five minutes while automatic releases are on, and reads CI through its GitHub App; the merges of those five minutes go out in one release of the newest green commit
  %%> What it accepts:
  %%> - a run of `ci.yml` on `main`, with `Main delivery checks`, its main `Required checks` result and `Gateway release inputs` green; duplicate main fixtures and Main full set report independently and never block delivery
  %%> - a run from a fork, a PR or another workflow does not count
  Note over GW: Admit the release<br/>one at a time
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - no other release queued or running, and automatic releases not paused
  %%> - the agent pin passes its Sigstore check; CI published the web build
  %%> Why:
  %%> - several merges can land during a release; the next run takes only the newest commit
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a running release record; the pin, artifact and targets are frozen as inputs
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-gateway-release
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the Gateway records intent only; Swamp executes. Detail of every step: chart `gateway:release:deploy`
  SW->>GN: Build the release<br/>composer · web build
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - refuses a commit that does not descend from the current release
  %%> - installs dependencies and the web build, and seals the release
  SW->>GN: Snapshot and migrate<br/>expand and contract
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes a database snapshot, then migrates while the old release still serves
  %%> - old code must work with the new schema
  SW->>GN: Wait for active Operations<br/>before Swamp load
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks release-blocking Operations while the old release and Horizon serve; force does not bypass it
  %%> - a busy timeout refuses with `gateway.release_busy`; no Swamp load or activation follows
  SW->>GN: Load the new workflows<br/>Swamp reloads, no restart
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the switch then runs the new commit's own steps
  SW->>GN: Drain Horizon<br/>loaded activation child
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - no switch follows a failed drain; Start Horizon still runs
  SW->>GN: Switch to the new release<br/>gateway-rollback script
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - switches the links, reloads PHP-FPM, restarts the running services; a failed switch still reaches Start Horizon
  SW->>GN: Check the Gateway<br/>health · version
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the health endpoint and the status version of the Gateway
  alt the check fails
    SW->>GN: Switch back<br/>gateway-rollback previous
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - returns to the previous release without Swamp; a failed switch-back reports its own error
  end
  SW->>GN: Start Horizon<br/>on the live release
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - always runs after activation paths, including failed drain, switch, verification or switch-back; skips only when no Horizon unit is configured
  %%> - a failed start admits no refresh
  alt verification and Horizon pass
    SW->>GN: Admit VM refreshes<br/>verified release's artisan
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - also permits a skipped Horizon start; admission is best effort and never waits for refresh completion (stage 6)
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
    Note over GW: Record the release<br/>verified
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Gateway admits the [Fleet rollout](/reference/gateway-recovery#fleet-rollout), and a daily pass at 03:05 Amsterdam visits the Nodes it deferred
    %%> - no fleet test follows a release; development defaults are not deployed by it
  else verification failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>switch-back result · alert
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Gateway records the failed verification and switch-back outcome; no refresh is admitted
  else a step from migrate on fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - from migrate on, the old release may be live with a changed schema, so the run stops and names the snapshot
    Note over GW: Pause automatic releases<br/>snapshot named · alert
    %%> Result:
    %%> - restoring the snapshot is an operator action; `gateway:auto-release:resume` clears the pause
  end
